<!--
    kuna `whilecontinue`: a jump to a loop's own test is `continue;`.  kuna
    printed `continue;` only in infinite loops, so in a do-while the jump from
    a switch arm to the block that holds nothing but the loop test printed
    `goto label_X;` and an empty `label_X: ;` above `} while (...)`.  With
    the option on (the default) a while-do (not a for) continues at its
    condition block and a do-while at a last leaf that prints only the test.

    Stage / sub-stage: P8 "goto-quality", option `whilecontinue on|off`.

    The bytes are little2_attributeValueTok from lib/xmltok.c of expat 2.8.2
    (MIT, after ./configure), built by gcc 15.3 at -O2 -fno-pie -no-pie
    -nostartfiles -nostdlib with unresolved symbols ignored, entry
    XmlInitEncoding; the function sits at 0x407f50 and its jump table at
    0x40ee40.  Pass 1 is the default, pass 2
    `option whilecontinue off`.
-->
